cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "c2pa-kyc-signing: A C2PA provenance signing service for KYC biometric capture"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Akwunte
    family-names: Amali
    affiliation: "MIVA Open University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Maliverse/c2pa-kyc-signing"
abstract: >-
  A reference implementation of C2PA content provenance signing applied to KYC
  biometric capture. Images are signed with Es256 (ECDSA P-256) and the manifest
  is embedded into the asset server-side, enabling verifiers to establish the
  origin of a submission rather than inferring authenticity from pixel content.
  Developed as the Layer 2 component of a trilayered architecture for
  deepfake-resistant identity verification.
keywords:
  - C2PA
  - content provenance
  - KYC
  - biometric verification
  - deepfake
  - injection attack
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-29
